  "description": "What: a vehicle leaves a warm patch where it idled (CE-4664, thermal drivers TD-14 / TD-S8; docs/designs/thermal/DESIGN_Thermal_Drivers.md \u00a74b; the thermal view draws it, DESIGN_Sensor_View \u00a75e). On basic-desert at 00:30 local, clear sky: 'Tank', a crewed T-72 at (300, 300), idles (a crewed vehicle starts Idle); 'Cold Truck', an HMMWV at (280, 300) in the SAME 64 m ground cell, is authored HeatSource Off (parked, engine cold). At 120 s the 'Drive Off' trigger orders both north to y = 500. Judge: the tank's engine ran for two minutes at its stand (>= the 60 s a stand needs), so when it moves off ONE heat mark is written to the cell's record (GroundHeatMarks, network id measured below) and the tank is Running; the truck's engine never ran there, so the record never holds a second mark. Fail: no mark, or two. Red-proof: author the truck Idle and the record holds two marks.",
